  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find $c$ for which the cubic equation $x^3-4x^2+bx+c=0$ has three positive integer roots.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=-2$.\n\nThe roots must be $1,1,2$, since their sum is $4$.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $p,q,r$. By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q+r&=4,\\\\pqr&=-c.\\end{align*}$$\nThe only three positive integers with sum $4$, allowing repeated roots, are $1,1,2$. Hence,\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=-pqr\\\\c&=-(1)(1)(2)\\\\c&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nIndeed, $(x-1)^2(x-2)=x^3-4x^2+5x-2$, so this value is possible.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
